            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Australia's Westpac profit grows 5% on margin lift and higher lending",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Australia's Westpac Banking Corp on Thursday said wider margins and lending and deposits gains helped it post slightly higher third-quarter profit, sending its shares surging more than 5%.  Westpac's net interest margins, the spread between interest earned from loans and paid to depositors, came in at 1.99% in the quarter, compared with 1.92% a year ago.  Net interest income was A$5 billion in the quarter, up 4% from the quarterly average in the first half.",
